                        "sense_id": "fdedacd6-6d5e-3fb0-b8f6-85fb31ddaeab",
                        "entry_id": "e6d9f830-01b2-31b5-99d8-3cd289359402",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The quality of something that matters; significance; importance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "de9c1d24-4832-4fec-9e74-36322209b28d",
                                "sense_id": "fdedacd6-6d5e-3fb0-b8f6-85fb31ddaeab",
                                "text": "But not all matterings matter the same: you value your daily respite at the coffee shop that's long brightened your mornings, but if that shop goes under, you wouldn't—I hope—be facing existential threat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f12ffeca-b6a5-4f22-be9c-b131c342d236",
                                "sense_id": "fdedacd6-6d5e-3fb0-b8f6-85fb31ddaeab",
                                "text": "Mattering is \"a core, universal human need,\" a necessary component for well-being, Dr. [Gordon] Flett said. But it's tricky to define, he added, because people sometimes confuse it with belonging, self-esteem and social connection."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
